    story: "Prague & Bohemian Castles forms a compact circuit through Czech river valleys and fortified towns. Prague begins on both banks of the Vltava, linking the castle precinct, Charles Bridge, Old Town and the modern civic layers beyond the postcard centre. The trail follows the Berounka toward Karlštejn, built by Charles IV to safeguard royal treasures. Konopiště introduces a later aristocratic residence associated with Archduke Franz Ferdinand, while Tábor's street plan recalls the Hussite movement. The southern section reaches Český Krumlov, where a vast castle and baroque theatre overlook a tight bend in the Vltava. Hluboká shows nineteenth-century romantic reconstruction, contrasting sharply with practical medieval strongholds. The return through Kutná Hora adds silver-mining history and the soaring church of Saint Barbara. By comparing royal, noble, military and industrial landscapes, the journey explains why castles changed function over time. Forest paths, river bends, breweries and small-town squares keep the scale intimate enough for a focused WalkQuest season.",
